  "body": "## What changed\r\n\r\n- **The program sim carries the machined body into the next setup.** When the program enters a setup that holds the part differently from the one before it, or one placed relative to it with #316's link (\"Same as\" included), the body the earlier setups left is moved through `setup_relative::transform_between`. The later setup starts from that body, not from a fresh block. #341/#326's refusal \"the program spans setups that hold the part differently\" is lifted for these programs.\r\n- **Engine** (`crates/sim/src/stock_sim/carry.rs`, new): `Body` is a two-sided column body, with a top (the existing dexel) and a floor per column. `LatticeTurn` reads the rigid transform. The carry re-indexes the lattice. It never re-samples.\r\n- **App walk** (`crates/app/src/stock_sim_carry.rs`, new): `simulate_document` walks the program through `carry::walk`. At each setup change it either carries or keeps the old clip. The verdict is read in the frame of the setup the program ends in. The M3.2 A clip moved here unchanged.\r\n- **`stock_sim::incoming_body(world, setup)`** returns the stock a setup starts from, in that setup's frame. #318 (rest) and #320 (incoming-stock display) can use it.\r\n\r\n## Design (per #308's research decision)\r\n\r\nThere is one body, viewed through each setup's transform. It is not re-sampled onto each setup's grid.\r\n- **Which turns carry exactly:** flips over X or Y, quarter turns about Z, and their products. These are the eight signed permutations that keep Z on +-Z. Each one maps every column centre exactly onto a column centre of the image lattice, so no value is interpolated.\r\n- **Two sides:** a flip swaps the sides (`top' = tz - floor`, `floor' = tz - top`). A column that was cut through stays cut through.\r\n- **Floor verdict:** once the floor has faced a tool (after a flip), it is judged against the part's bottom, so a gouge cut before the flip is still judged after it. A body that is never flipped gets exactly the old one-sided verdict.\r\n- **Carry vs clip:** two setups that hold the part the same way and are not linked keep the M3.2 A clip. This is #320's planned default, before #320 makes it a per-setup choice.\r\n- **Incoming stock:** a carried setup's own stock entity is not read by the sim. Its incoming stock is the carried body.\r\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/317-carry-body.md`.\r\n\r\n## What is refused (by name)\r\n\r\n- A turn the lattice cannot carry exactly: side-on, Z turns off the quarter, mirrors. The refusal is `CARRY_TURN_REFUSAL` and names both setups.\r\n- A lathe or mill-turn machine.\r\n- Lathe, rotary and posed programs, refused before the walk as before.\r\n- Setups with different machines (#390's refusal, unchanged).\r\n- The field view and playback still draw one setup only. Their refusal text now says the program verdict carries the stock.\r\n\r\n## Readings\r\n\r\n- **Flip over X** (stock Z -2..18, part Z 0..16, Setup1 faces to 16): Setup2's incoming body spans Z 0..18 and holds 60x60x18 = 64800 mm³ exactly. The 2 mm Setup1 removed is absent from below. After Setup2 faces the former bottom to 16, the verdict is clean on both sides, and every column matches a single-frame reference (block Z 0..18 faced to 16) within DEV_TOL.\r\n- **Gouge before the flip:** Setup1 faces to 15, 1 mm into the part. After the flip the verdict reads a gouge of exactly 1.0 mm at Z 1, on the floor side.\r\n- **Quarter turn:** the 60x40 block lies 40x60, Setup1's face stays on top at 16, the volume is unchanged and the verdict is clean.\r\n- **Identity:** Setup2 linked \"Same as Setup1\" gives the same verdict, bit for bit, as both faces in one setup.\r\n\r\n## Pinning tests\r\n\r\n- `crates/sim/tests/stock_carry.rs` (new, 6 tests):\r\n  - `identity_carries_the_body_onto_itself`\r\n  - `a_flip_over_x_swaps_the_sides_exactly_and_twice_is_home`\r\n  - `a_quarter_turn_reindexes_the_lattice_and_four_are_home`\r\n  - `turns_the_lattice_cannot_carry_are_refused_by_name`\r\n  - `a_flipped_body_is_judged_on_both_sides`\r\n  - `a_column_cut_through_is_air_to_the_eye_and_a_gouge_to_the_verdict`\r\n- `crates/app/tests/setup_carry.rs` (new, 5 tests):\r\n  - `a_flipped_setup_starts_from_what_the_first_one_cut`\r\n  - `a_gouge_cut_before_the_flip_is_still_judged_after_it`\r\n  - `a_quarter_turn_carries_the_body_reindexed`\r\n  - `a_setup_linked_same_as_the_first_carries_the_body_unchanged`\r\n  - `a_turn_the_lattice_cannot_carry_is_refused_by_name`\r\n- `crates/app/tests/setup_align.rs`: `the_program_sim_refuses_by_name_across_differently_held_setups` is now `the_program_sim_carries_the_stock_across_differently_held_setups`. That behaviour changed on purpose.\r\n\r\n## Gate (on the tree merged with current main)\r\n\r\n- sim: `stock_carry` (6), `stock_sim` (24), `stock_columns`, `stock_backend_parity` - all green\r\n- app: lib (95), `setup_carry` (5), `setup_align` (9), `setup_relative` (8), `setups` (11), `stock_sim_document` (9), `posting` (17), `golden_cl` (23, goldens unchanged), `post_not_judged` (4), `lathe_field_sim` (6), `rotary_field_parity` (3 + 1 ignored heavy lane) - all green\r\n- clippy `-D warnings` on camcraft-sim and camcraft-app, all targets: clean\r\n\r\nChangelog: The program sim carries the machined stock into the next setup through the setup transform (flips over X/Y, quarter turns about Z), so a later setup starts from what the earlier one cut and a gouge cut before a flip is still reported; other turns are refused by name.\r\n\r\nBuilds on #397 (merged).\r\n\r\nFixes #317\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n",
